      "role": "user",
      "content": "The part about \"finding meaning again\" just feels so hollow. I'm not looking for a new hobby or a way to fill the time. I mean, if you're watching a movie and the climax has passed and the screen goes black, you don't sit there for another two hours waiting for something to happen. The story is over. It feels more like I'm just lingering in the credits of a movie that's already finished. Why do people insist that there has to be a sequel when the original was everything?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
